# Fixed stage-frame cohort patch

`stage-runtime-cohort.patch` is unapplied. It changes `src/game/services/stage-runtime.ts` and adds `tests/stage-runtime-cohort.test.ts`. Only this ignored directory was written during preparation.

## Contract and scope

Each logical fixed frame takes one recipient cohort before `MainEffects.tick`. Both `beforeStep` and `step` use that cohort. A listener created during effects, `beforeStep` or `step` begins frame callbacks in the next logical frame, including a later catch-up frame within the same `advance` call. Membership is checked before every hook, so removal before a pending invocation still suppresses it; self-removal in `beforeStep` suppresses its later `step`.

Elapsed-time callbacks and draw iteration deliberately retain their existing live-Set semantics. A newly attached menu can draw in its birth frame without receiving its first Run. Drawing happens once after catch-up, not once per fixed frame. A subscription created during draw can draw in that same pass as before. These are preserved application contracts, not claims about every Flash render traversal behavior.

Membership uses listener-object identity, without registration epochs. Removing and re-adding the same listener object does not make it a new object for this cohort. The patch fixes fresh-listener entry and preserves current removal behavior; it does not emulate all AVM2 object buckets, per-target listener priorities, weak references, or handler-list snapshots.

## Source evidence and limits

Original Main.Run case3 calls World.Run (`Main.as549–552`). `BTAGameWorld._-3F` constructs the new menu and registers its Run through Setup while that earlier listener is executing (`BTAGameWorld.as1403–1411`, `UpgradeMenu.as675–676`).

The inspected Ruffle v0.7.1 source appends new recipient objects at `core/src/avm2.rs398` and fixes the bucket length before dispatch at423–430. A fresh menu registered during Main's callback is beyond that broadcast's fixed range. Per-target handlers are collected before invocation at `core/src/avm2/events.rs386–390`.

